Chapter: GuardPageProbe
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Fires the heap guard page. `park-bytes` and `reserve-bytes` are substituted by
 `build/guard-page-test.ps1`; the arms differ in those two values and in nothing
 else.

 `burn` allocates in small steps on purpose. A 2 MB guard page catches a bump
 that lands INSIDE it, so a single allocation larger than 2 MB steps clean over
 the hole -- which is why the incremental arms walk up in ~40-byte pieces.

 The other failure class -- a deck reservation leaping the page in one advance --
 cannot be probed from here: `build` lives in the compiler's own unit
 (`Core/PhaseAllocator.codex`) and an app cannot cite it. That arm drives the
 real compiler at an inflated `-Decks` instead; see `guard-page-test.ps1`.

Section: Definitions

  burn : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  burn (acc) (n) =
   if n <= 0 then acc
   else let s = "0123456789012345678901234567890" & show n
    in burn (acc + text-length s) (n - 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
   let parked = __heap-advance park-bytes
   in act
    print-line-uni ("parked: " & show parked)
    print-line-uni ("burned: " & show (burn 0 100000))
    print-line-uni "SURVIVED"
   end
  end
